{"seconds": 0.21788841695524752, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-extension-v1/submissions/E06/gpt-5-2025-08-07.json", "submission_sha256": "7e7c2960e445aaee896795b8c5b36eb4ed0990e334fb2c59dc8f0400ab1b4620", "code_sha256": "3e5259ef60034c5ecf8bbe9c7ed7d9593b83d3a43c52d9b6ac9d3fe213e56f86", "description": "Analytic NLinear-style forecaster with training-only fitting and per-horizon shrinkage.\n- Pool every neuron and window: for each (example, neuron), form a 64-D history vector and a 32-D target.\n- Subtract the last observed frame from both history and target to learn future deltas.\n- Fit a shared temporal affine map (64\u219232) with ridge regularization (alpha=1.0) and an unpenalized bias using closed-form normal equations on training data only.\n- Calibrate a per-horizon shrinkage factor gamma (size 32) by least-squares mixing against the naive \"repeat last frame\" baseline, clipped to [0,1] for stability.\n- Predict on test: subtract last frame, apply the affine map, shrink deltas by gamma, and add the last frame back. If any numerical issue occurs, fall back to repeating the last input frame.\n- Deterministic, NumPy-only, vectorized across all neurons and windows; returns finite outputs with shape (len(test_x), 32, 256).", "code_lines": 142, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

